fix(startup): use a timer instead of rAF to reveal the window

The previous commit revealed the main window from a double
requestAnimationFrame. That never fires while the window is hidden, and the
main window starts with `visible: false` — so the reveal callback was never
scheduled, `app_show_main_window` was never called, and the app appeared not
to start at all.

A timer has no such precondition. `ready` is committed before it is armed,
so the first view is already rendered when the window is finally shown.

Verified by launching the built binary and checking the window directly:
Visible=True, 1518x885, process responding.